title: Start
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 2
position: 0,0
---
This lesson is about input replies. An "input" command inside a reply collects a value from the user and stores it in a variable.

What is your first name?

[[My name is <<input type="text" value="$inName" min="2" max="30" description="your first name">>.|LongText]]
===
title: LongText
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 320,0
---
Thank you, $inName. The "longtext" type is meant for multi-line answers.

[[<<input type="longtext" value="$inBio" description="a short bio">>|Email]]
===
title: Email
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 640,0
---
The "email" type collects an address.

[[My address is <<input type="email" value="$inEmail">>.|Numeric]]
===
title: Numeric
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 960,0
---
The "numeric" type collects a number and accepts a range.

[[I am <<input type="numeric" value="$inAge" min="0" max="120">> years old.|Time]]
===
title: Time
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 1280,0
---
The "time" type collects a time of day, with an optional step and range.

[[I woke up at <<input type="time" value="$inWakeTime" granularityMinutes="15" startTime="07:00" minTime="04:00" maxTime="12:00">> today.|Set]]
===
title: Set
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 1600,0
---
The "set" type shows a group of labelled options, each toggling its own boolean variable.

[[I would like <<input type="set" value1="$inCheese" option1="Cheese" value2="$inOlives" option2="Olives" value3="$inHam" option3="Ham">> on it.|End]]
===
title: End
tags:
speaker:
colorId: 5
position: 800,220
---

===
